@@ -82,6 +83,9 @@ Network file systems like Samba and NFS are not supported. Microsoft Dev Drives
 When enabled by default, file system watching acts conservatively when it encounters content on unsupported file systems.
 This can happen if you mount a project directory or subdirectory from a network drive.
 Gradle doesn't retain information about unsupported file systems between builds when enabled by default.
+The Android distribution classifies each location by its nearest mounted file system, so supported nested mounts remain eligible beneath unsupported ancestors.
+Unsupported or remote nested mounts remain excluded, and an ambiguous mount table disables default watching rather than guessing mount visibility.
+When a mount changes, retained state below that mount is invalidated before reuse.
 If you explicitly enable file system watching, Gradle retains information about unsupported file systems between builds.
 
